  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 216 PM MDT SAT SEP 12 2026\nA broad trough remains in place over the region. This will \nallow a weak upper level trough and accompanying dry cold front \nto cross the area. Limited moisture will keep precipitation \nchances near zero, but the frontal passage will generate breezy \nconditions, especially across the Snake River Plain and high \nterrain. High temperatures on Tuesday will remain slightly below\nseasonal normals behind the front.\n\nBy Wednesday, an upper level ridge begins building over the\nIntermountain West. Heights and temperatures aloft will steadily\nincrease through the end of the week, yielding a clear warming\nand drying trend from Wednesday through Saturday. Temperatures\nwill rise to 5 to 10 degrees above normal by Friday and\nSaturday. Model guidance shows high confidence in stable\nconditions under the ridge, with light diurnal winds and minimal\ncloud cover prevailing across the region through the remainder\nof the period.",
